hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"20961","Affan narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to me, he said: I heard Amr ibn Salamah say: When the day of the conquest came, the people began passing us having come from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I used to recite while a boy, and my father came with the Islam of his people to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let lead you the most Quran among you. They looked and I was the most Quran among them. He said: A woman said: Cover the backside of your reciter. He said: They bought him a cloak. He said: I never rejoiced more severely than my joy with that."
"20962","Abd al-Wahid ibn Wasil al-Haddad narrated to us, Misar Abu al-Harith al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: I heard Amr ibn Salamah al-Jarmi narrating that his father and a group of his people came as a delegation to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when his matter appeared and the people learned, and they fulfilled their needs, then asked him: Who prays for us or prays with us. He said: Let pray for you or with you the most of you in gathering the Quran or taking the Quran. They came to their people and asked in the tribe and found none who had gathered more than I had gathered, so they put me forward before them and I prayed with them while a boy with a shawl upon me. He said: I never attended a gathering of Jarm but I was their imam to this day of mine."
"20963","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us from Abu Qilabah from Amr ibn Salamah who said: Riders used to come to us from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and we would have them recite to us, and they would narrate to us that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let lead you the most Quran among you."
